"1\n00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,529\nThe Learning Brain. Series 5: Belonging\n\n2\n00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:07,333\nEpisode 2\n\n3\n00:00:07,413 --> 00:00:09,394\nBelonging at scale\n\n4\n00:00:12,194 --> 00:00:17,430\nA one hour exercise that halves an achievement gap sounds almost too good to be true.\n\n5\n00:00:17,886 --> 00:00:20,694\nSo researchers did what good science does.\n\n6\n00:00:21,055 --> 00:00:22,148\nThey tested it again,\n\n7\n00:00:22,168 --> 00:00:23,165\nand much bigger.\n\n8\n00:00:23,335 --> 00:00:26,106\nFirst, a follow up of the original students,\n\n9\n00:00:26,267 --> 00:00:30,870\nyears later, reported better adult outcomes for the Black participants.\n\n10\n00:00:31,279 --> 00:00:33,360\nBut that was still one small group,\n\n11\n00:00:33,426 --> 00:00:34,722\non one campus.\n\n12\n00:00:34,892 --> 00:00:45,272\nSo in 2023, a large team ran the exercise with twenty six thousand nine hundred and eleven students at twenty two colleges and universities.\n\n13\n00:00:45,729 --> 00:00:48,517\nStudents did it online before college began,\n\n14\n00:00:48,846 --> 00:00:50,300\nin under thirty minutes.\n\n15\n00:00:50,470 --> 00:00:55,280\nIt raised the share of students who completed their first year as full time students,\n\n16\n00:00:55,577 --> 00:00:59,790\nespecially in groups that had historically progressed at lower rates.\n\n17\n00:01:00,281 --> 00:01:06,899\nThe researchers estimated the results could generalize to seven hundred and forty nine four year institutions.\n\n18\n00:01:07,277 --> 00:01:11,138\nAnd the online materials are freely available to colleges.\n\n19\n00:01:11,308 --> 00:01:13,057\nBut here is the key finding.\n\n20\n00:01:13,457 --> 00:01:17,638\nIt only worked where students' groups actually had opportunities to belong.\n\n21\n00:01:18,134 --> 00:01:22,273\nA message about belonging cannot create belonging that isn't there.\n\n22\n00:01:22,720 --> 00:01:25,371\nIn other words, the message has to be true.\n\n23\n00:01:25,541 --> 00:01:26,525\nSome caution.\n\n24\n00:01:26,910 --> 00:01:29,672\nThe effects were smaller than in the original study.\n\n25\n00:01:30,003 --> 00:01:31,031\nThat is normal: large,\n\n26\n00:01:31,311 --> 00:01:35,031\ncareful studies usually shrink early results.\n\n27\n00:01:35,305 --> 00:01:37,534\nAnd small effects, across many students,\n\n28\n00:01:37,554 --> 00:01:38,695\ncan still matter.\n\n29\n00:01:38,865 --> 00:01:39,619\nFor teaching.\n\n30\n00:01:39,930 --> 00:01:41,643\nShare the belonging message early,\n\n31\n00:01:41,663 --> 00:01:43,142\nbefore the first setbacks.\n\n32\n00:01:43,397 --> 00:01:44,274\nThen back it up.\n\n33\n00:01:44,751 --> 00:01:47,331\nBuild study groups, learn students' names,\n\n34\n00:01:47,351 --> 00:01:50,342\nand hold office hours students actually use.\n\n35\n00:01:50,660 --> 00:01:53,099\nLook at who leaves your course,\n\n36\n00:01:53,496 --> 00:01:55,310\nand ask why.\n\n37\n00:01:55,548 --> 00:01:59,019\nOne tip to share with students: join one group or activity in your first few weeks.\n\n38\n00:01:59,189 --> 00:02:00,808\nTell students they belong.\n\n39\n00:02:01,070 --> 00:02:03,039\nThen build the course that proves it.\n\n"
